---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Phone Mic to Bluetooth Speaker Privacy Policy - LogicPath Systems">
    <section class="legal-page" style="padding-top: 120px; min-height: 100vh;">
        <div class="container reveal">
            <div class="glass-card" style="padding: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem);">
                <header style="margin-bottom: 3rem; text-align: center;">
                    <h1 class="gradient-text">Privacy Policy</h1>
                    <p style="color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;"><strong>Phone Mic to Bluetooth Speaker</strong></p>
                    <p style="color: var(--text-secondary);">Logic Path Systems &middot; <strong>Effective date:</strong> 29 October 2026</p>
                </header>

                <main class="legal-content">
                    <p>This policy explains what Phone Mic to Bluetooth Speaker (&ldquo;the app&rdquo;), published by Logic Path Systems, does with information on your phone. In short: your voice is never recorded or uploaded. The app shows ads from Google AdMob and uses Google Firebase to understand how the app is used.</p>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>Microphone and your voice</h2>
                    <p>The app uses the microphone only while you open it (tap Open mic or hold it to talk). Your voice goes straight from the microphone to the speaker you choose, in real time.</p>
                    <p>Your voice is not recorded, saved, or sent anywhere. Gain, the noise filter, echo cancel, auto level and the feedback guard all run on your phone.</p>
                    <p>To pause the mic during a phone or internet call, the app checks your phone's audio mode. It does not read call details, numbers or contacts.</p>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>Permissions</h2>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Microphone:</strong> needed to pass your voice to the speaker. Used only while the mic is open.</li>
                        <li><strong>Notifications:</strong> shows the ongoing &ldquo;Phone Mic is open&rdquo; notification with Mute and Stop buttons while the mic runs in the background.</li>
                        <li><strong>Audio devices and Bluetooth:</strong> the app lists your connected speakers so you can pick one. Device names stay on your phone.</li>
                    </ul>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>Announcements (cues)</h2>
                    <p>Cues you write are saved only on your phone. When you play one, the text is spoken by the text-to-speech engine installed on your phone. Some engines or voices may process text under their own provider's privacy policy.</p>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>Stored on your phone</h2>
                    <p>Your cues, settings (such as noise filter and chime choices) and simple usage totals (time with the mic open, sessions and cues played) are kept in the app's private storage. They are not uploaded. Clearing the app's data or uninstalling it deletes them.</p>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>Advertising (Google AdMob)</h2>
                    <p>The app shows ads from Google AdMob. To show, measure and protect ads against fraud, AdMob may collect your device's advertising ID, IP address, approximate location based on IP, device and app information, ad interactions, and crash or diagnostic data.</p>
                    <p>Where the law requires it (for example in the EEA, UK and Switzerland), the app asks for your consent before personalised ads are shown. In those regions an Ad privacy options button appears in Options so you can change that choice at any time. You can also reset or delete your advertising ID in your phone's Android settings.</p>
                    <p>Ads are never shown while the mic is open or a cue is playing.</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>How Google uses data from partner apps: <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" style="color: var(--accent-secondary);" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites</a></li>
                        <li>Google Privacy Policy: <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" style="color: var(--accent-secondary);" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://policies.google.com/privacy</a></li>
                    </ul>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>Analytics (Google Firebase)</h2>
                    <p>The app uses Google Firebase Analytics to understand how the app is used, for example which features are opened, app version, device model, Android version, country or region, and an app instance ID. The app also uses Firebase Remote Config to adjust settings such as how often ads appear.</p>
                    <p>Your voice, your cue text and your speaker names are never sent to Firebase. You can reset the app instance ID by clearing the app's data.</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Privacy and security in Firebase: <a href="https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy" style="color: var(--accent-secondary);" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy</a></li>
                    </ul>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>Children</h2>
                    <p>The app is not directed at children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from them.</p>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>Your choices</h2>
                    <p>Where consent applies, you can turn off personalised ads in Options &gt; Ad privacy options. You can also reset your advertising ID in Android settings, clear the app's data, or uninstall the app at any time. Data sent to Google services is transferred over encrypted connections and handled under Google's policies linked above.</p>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
                    <p>If this policy changes, the new version will appear in the app and on its store listing with a new effective date.</p>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>Contact</h2>
                    <p><a href="mailto:contact@logicpathsystems.com" style="color: var(--accent-secondary);">contact@logicpathsystems.com</a></p>
                </main>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
</Layout>

<style>
    .legal-content h2 {
        color: var(--text-primary);
        margin-top: 2.5rem;
        margin-bottom: 1rem;
        font-size: 1.5rem;
    }

    .legal-content h3 {
        color: var(--text-primary);
        margin-top: 1.5rem;
        margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
        font-size: 1.25rem;
    }

    .legal-content p, .legal-content ul {
        color: var(--text-secondary);
        margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
        font-size: 1.05rem;
        line-height: 1.7;
    }

    .legal-content ul {
        padding-left: 2rem;
        margin-bottom: 2rem;
    }

    .legal-content li {
        margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    }
</style>

